{
  "_note": "case-search-declares-its-fields (rows 9.2, 9.1 and 9.12). The consumer half of openregister search-quality-operators-and-facets (#3768, #3806). Every case property a person searches or filters on says HOW: `matchType` is one of exact, prefix, range, fuzzy or fulltext, and `inputControl` is one of text, select, multiselect, range, date-range or boolean, both read by OCA\\OpenRegister\\Service\\Search\\PropertySearchProfile and answered to a list surface as searchable_fields[<prop>] under ?_facetable=true. ONE DECLARATION SERVES THE LIST, THE FACET, THE API AND THE PORTAL: put it in a page config instead and four surfaces get four answers, three of which drift. A BOOLEAN DECLARES ITS CONTROL AND NEVER A MATCH TYPE, and neither do the object properties and the JSON blobs held in a string (properties, statusHistory, casePlanState, geometry, relatedCases, skippedPhases, missingFields, activity and their kin). This is not a preference: PropertySearchProfile::participatesInFreeText() asks a DIFFERENT question of a declared property than of a silent one, and a declared match type other than `range` enlists the column in the free-text scan. Declaring `exact` on isDraft would make a search for the word \"true\" return every draft, and `range` on a boolean is a lie. Design D-3 asks openregister for a sixth value that means filterable but never scanned. THREE DECLARATIONS DELIBERATELY NARROW AN EXISTING SEARCH (design D-4): identifier and initiatorSourceId stop answering to half a case number or half a BSN, and the uuid references stop being substring-scanned. `tags` moves the other way: an array never joined the scan, and `fuzzy` puts it in so that \"spoedd\" finds \"spoed\". A FRAGMENT RATHER THAN THE MONOLITH (ADR-037) so the diff reads as what changed, and no info.version bump: SettingsService::readEffectiveConfiguration() records that openregister now hashes the merged configuration and skips on hash equality, so new content here forces the re-import on its own.",
